############ arm 2: intact + HD_SEQ_BREAK_DRAIN (destructive) ############
#  Skips the write drain only. The mode-A re-issue is left alone, so this
#  arm fails on the DRAIN or not at all -- it can no longer die of
#  starvation and be scored as a catch.
#
#  ?”´ WHETHER IT CAN FAIL AT ALL IS A MEASUREMENT, NOT AN ASSUMPTION.
#  The race needs the residual write drain (e_done -> m_out_done) to
#  outlast the gap to the next e_start. Arm 1 prints both numbers as
#  DRAINRACE reachable=/maxdrain=/maxgap=, and the verdict below REQUIRES
#  this arm to fail only when reachable=1. Measured 2026-08-15: it is 0 --
#  twn_axi_wr has no write FIFO and tb_ddr_model answers B on wlast, so
#  the drain is a couple of cycles while the requant reload alone is ~68.
#  That is a fact about this bench, and the rule turns itself back on if a
#  FIFO or a real interconnect ever changes it. The directed test for the
#  race is tb_hd_seq.v check 3, which holds the drain off for 200 cycles.
